  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Where is East Newton?",
      "a": "In Surrey's Newton community — the City describes East Newton as the neighbourhoods around Chimney Hill, east of 144 Street, north of 64 Avenue and Hyland Creek, and south of Bear Creek, planned through the East Newton North, East Newton South and East Newton Business Park NCPs.",
      "gen": "muse"
    },
    {
      "q": "What plans govern East Newton now?",
      "a": "The 1990s NCPs planned the subdivisions and the area is now largely built out, but the City states East Newton North was rescinded and East Newton South's and the Business Park's designations were superseded by the Surrey 2050 Official Community Plan update — read the current OCP and Zoning Bylaw, not just the old NCP documents.",
      "gen": "muse"
    },
    {
      "q": "How many homes are for sale in East Newton?",
      "a": "At the end of October 2026 the Fraser Valley Real Estate Board figures showed 110 houses listed with 16 sold in the month and 113 condos and townhomes listed with 20 sold in the month in East Newton. Those are month-end counts and move daily; ask Jared what is on the market today.",
      "gen": "snap-faq"
    },
    {
      "q": "Is East Newton a buyers’ or sellers’ market?",
      "a": "In October 2026, houses had a sales ratio of 15%, a balanced market; condos and townhomes had a sales ratio of 18%, a balanced market. On the reports’ scale under 12% favours buyers, 12% to 20% is balanced and over 20% favours sellers.",
      "gen": "snap-faq"
    }
  ]
}
